From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:45:24 +0800
Subject: xcursor: fix discarded const qualifier

Keep the path separator pointer const when parsing Xcursor search paths. This avoids a -Werror=discarded-qualifiers failure with current compilers.
---
 xcursor/xcursor.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xcursor/xcursor.c b/xcursor/xcursor.c
index b5edb9d..6627fb6 100644
--- a/xcursor/xcursor.c
+++ b/xcursor/xcursor.c
@@ -602,7 +602,7 @@ xcursor_build_fullname(const char *dir, const char *subdir, const char *file)
 static const char *
 xcursor_next_path(const char *path)
 {
-	char *colon = strchr(path, ':');
+	const char *colon = strchr(path, ':');
 
 	if (!colon)
 		return NULL;
